Package: gnome-shell-extension-psi-monitor
Version: @VERSION@
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: gnome-shell (>= 46~), gnome-shell (<< 47~)
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Homepage: @HOMEPAGE@
Description: CPU, memory, disk and GPU badges for the GNOME top bar
 Shows colored badges in the top bar for disk, CPU, memory and GPU, plus
 Wi-Fi and Ethernet speed. For disk, CPU and memory the badge shows how much
 of the resource is in use, and its color (green, yellow or red) comes from
 the kernel's Pressure Stall Information (PSI), so it reflects whether tasks
 are actually stalling and not only how busy the resource is.
 .
 A menu shows PSI over 10 seconds, 60 seconds and 5 minutes, per-disk busy
 time and throughput, CPU, RAM and swap usage, Wi-Fi and Ethernet link state
 and speed, and NVIDIA GPU usage, VRAM and temperature when nvidia-smi is
 available.
 .
 Requires GNOME Shell 46, as shipped by Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. After installing,
 restart GNOME Shell and enable the extension with gnome-extensions enable.
